## Report
Code inspection shows `with_bucket_write_handle_for` loads a snapshot under `with_bucket_write_snapshot` and then runs the caller action *after* that snapshot call returns (crates/server-core/src/coordinator/authz.rs:1713-1734). The storage layer releases the write reservation immediately after the snapshot/action closure completes (crates/storage/src/node.rs:692-707). Bucket deletion waits only for `active_write_reservations` to reach zero (crates/server-core/src/coordinator/bucket.rs:290-303; crates/server-core/src/coordinator/infra.rs:211-229). I added a targeted unit test that blocks inside the write action while a concurrent `delete_bucket` runs; `cargo test -p server-core delete_bucket_can_race_write_handle_action -- --nocapture` panics because `delete_bucket` returns Ok while the write action is still blocked, demonstrating the reservation no longer covers the actual write action.

