## Narrative
The coordinator now loads a bucket handle under a write snapshot and then executes the caller’s write action after with_bucket_write_snapshot returns (authz.rs:1713-1734). In storage, the write reservation is released immediately after the snapshot action completes (node.rs:692-707). Bucket deletion waits only for active_write_reservations to reach zero (bucket.rs:290-303; infra.rs:211-229), so it can complete while the write action is still running. The provided PoC test demonstrates this race by panicking when delete_bucket finishes before the write action completes. The issue is reachable via normal S3 write/delete operations but requires authenticated privileges and a race condition; impact is integrity-only and, per the threat model, typically confined to the same tenant.
## Controls
- SigV4-style authenticated access via configured credential store
- authorize_delete_bucket access control check
- Bucket write reservations and drain logic
## Blindspots
- No deployment manifests to confirm whether the service is exposed publicly or remains localhost-only.
- Multi-tenant account support not evidenced; cross-owner bucket recreation impact remains speculative.
- Static analysis only; no end-to-end network PoC executed in this environment.
